popcorn container image

This image holds the popcorn Python package, its pytest extra and uv, on top of
the python:3.14-slim-trixie base image.

popcorn
  The licence of popcorn and of every component it builds in is in LICENSE,
  NOTICE and LICENSES/ in this directory, the same files as the package's
  dist-info. The extension links Unicorn statically, so the installed package
  is a combined work subject to GPL-2.0-only. The exact source is the popcorn
  git commit named in the image label org.opencontainers.image.revision, at
  https://github.com/Garcia6l20/popcorn, submodules included. The Unicorn
  source is the fork commit that the third_party/unicorn submodule of that
  revision pins, from https://github.com/Garcia6l20/unicorn, branch popcorn.
  NOTICE lists the fork's changes to upstream Unicorn with their dates.

GCC 16.2.0 runtime libraries
  /usr/local/lib/libstdc++.so.6.0.36, /usr/local/lib/libgcc_s.so.1 and
  /usr/local/lib/libatomic.so.1.2.0 are copied unmodified from GCC 16.2.0.
  They are licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 with the
  GCC Runtime Library Exception version 3.1, texts in gcc-runtime/COPYING3 and
  gcc-runtime/COPYING.RUNTIME. Source:
  https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gcc/gcc-16.2.0/gcc-16.2.0.tar.xz

uv
  Installed from PyPI into the system Python, dual licensed MIT or Apache-2.0.
  Texts in /usr/local/lib/python3.14/site-packages/uv-*.dist-info/licenses/.

Base image
  The Debian packages of the base image carry their copyright files under
  /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.

STM32 data
  The image holds the two shipped part descriptions inside the popcorn
  package, with the attribution in NOTICE. It holds no STM32CubeMX database
  and no copy of STM32_open_pin_data. Other parts are built from an ST
  installation the user mounts into the container.
